{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:aa8b4e87dff8b63b","name":"Jumpstar HPF Starfighter","source":{"id":"source:reference-aa8b4e87dff8b63b","title":"Jumpstar HPF Starfighter","revision":20225,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T23:26:32Z","sha256":"a13bebb3fa8c5b4c1577b853e75195432ecd6f9df45cf41b5f07ffaa146c63e4","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20225","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Jumpstar%20HPF%20Starfighter&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-aa8b4e87dff8b63b","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Legacy Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Legacy_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Twisted Star Squadron"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Twisted_Star_Squadron","referenceId":"reference:f9be71416f8fe069"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:bd53073ee6d4d9a0"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Jumpstar Hyperspace Pursuit Fighter is a sleet ship with dual engines flanking a central cockpit and a pair of retractable sensor arrays that span between the engines, arcing over and under them. The fighter's primary duty is to pursue fleeing ships through Hyperspace, making it popular among military organizations and law enforcement agencies that must track fleeing targets regularly. In addition to its sophisticated sensors and exceptional ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"},", the Jumpstar is also an excellent pursuit fighter. Though not quite as fast as the best interceptors, the ship performs well against other topline fighters.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Jumpstars successfully track targets by one of two methods. The most reliable way is to tag a target with an S-thread or other hyperspace tracking device, usually fired from the attacking fighter via a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Marker Missile"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Marker_Missile"},". While large ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," or freighters are easy to tag, fighters, shuttles, and other small craft are more difficult to hit. The second method is less reliable, as it depends on the fighter's own sensor array and navigational computer to analyze a fleeing ship's departure vector, engine output, and other data that might tip off its final destination. Often such calculations must be made with great speed, and the pilot must make some educated guesses and assumptions when presented with a list of possible destinations. Plotting hyperspace jumps at great speed is always a risky business.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["To trace a fleeing ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," with a tracking device attached, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," must make a DC 15 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check. To track a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," without a homing beacon, the Jumpstar (or another Jumpstar) must have observed the ship's departure into hyperspace, and the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," must make a DC 25 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check (with a -2 penalty for each ",{"tag":"a","children":["Range"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Range"}," increment beyond Short in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Scale"},"). In either case, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," adds the ship's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intelligence"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intelligence"}," modifier to the roll. After this roll is made, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," must still make a standard ",{"tag":"a","children":["Astrogate"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Astrogate"}," check to initiative the pursuit.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Skilled"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Jumpstar HPF Starfighter Statistics (CL 9)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Gargantuan ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +7; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 18 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 12), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 24; +7 Armor, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicular Combat"],"href":"https://swse.mira